# Oscillitron demo configuration — .properties format.
#
# CLAUDE GENERATED
#
# This file fills in any setting the user did NOT pass as a CLI flag.
# CLI flags always win. Lines starting with '#' or '!' are comments;
# duplicate keys: last write wins.
#
# Use:
#   go run ./cmd/oscillitron --config oscillitron.properties
#   OSCILLITRON_CONFIG=oscillitron.properties go run ./cmd/oscillitron

# ----- Single-endpoint case: one Hermes serves every brain function.
# (Easiest for v0 dev — point at one local `hermes gateway` on :8642.)

# hermes.url=http://127.0.0.1:8642
# hermes.model=openrouter:openai/gpt-4o-mini

# ----- Multi-endpoint case: one Hermes PER brain function.
# (Matches the locked architecture — each specialist's persistent
# store is its own long-lived Hermes process. Spawn N gateways on
# different ports and bind them here.)
#
# When ANY hermes.endpoints.* entry is present, the single-endpoint
# settings above are ignored.

# hermes.endpoints.planning.url=http://127.0.0.1:8642
# hermes.endpoints.planning.model=openrouter:openai/gpt-4o-mini
# hermes.endpoints.reasoning.url=http://127.0.0.1:8643
# hermes.endpoints.reasoning.model=openrouter:openai/gpt-4o-mini
# hermes.endpoints.retrieval.url=http://127.0.0.1:8644
# hermes.endpoints.retrieval.model=openrouter:openai/gpt-4o-mini
# hermes.endpoints.critic.url=http://127.0.0.1:8645
# hermes.endpoints.critic.model=openrouter:anthropic/claude-3.5-haiku

# ----- Misc.

# timeout=5m
